
 OPENSWOS for the Amiga
 =========================

 Sensible World of Soccer, rebuilt in C from the original Amiga game, so
 that one source code runs on the Amiga, Windows, macOS, Linux, the web
 and more. Same game, same feel: the aim is to play exactly as the
 original Amiga release did.

 Reverse engineered, ported to C and AGA version by Ben Baker (benbaker76),
 ben@baker76.com

 "Sensible World of Soccer" (C) 1994-97 Sensible Software.
 OpenSWOS is a fan project and is not affiliated with Sensible Software
 or its current rights holders.

 Downloads, the other versions and the changelog:
        https://baker76.com/swos.html


 WHAT YOU NEED
 -------------

 - An AGA Amiga with a 68020 or better: an A1200 or A4000, or an
   emulator set up as one (FS-UAE, WinUAE).
 - A hard drive, and Workbench to start it from.


 INSTALLING
 ----------

 Unpack the archive onto your hard drive as it is. You get a SWOS drawer
 with its icon. Open the drawer and double-click SWOS.

 Everything the game needs is inside the drawer, so it can live anywhere:
 move it as a whole, never the files one by one.

 Saved careers, seasons, tactics and highlights go in the "save" drawer.


 BOOTING AN EMULATOR STRAIGHT INTO THE GAME
 -----------------------------------------

 Point the emulator's boot hard drive at the SWOS drawer itself. Its own
 startup-sequence (in s) starts the game, and leaving the game closes the
 emulator. The c and s drawers do nothing when you start the game from
 Workbench.


 WHAT IS IN THE DRAWER
 ---------------------

 SWOS          what the icon starts (a one-line script that runs SWOS2)
 SWOS2         the game
 data          teams, competitions and the rest of the game's data
 grafs         graphics
 grafs_aga     AGA graphics
 sound         music and sound effects
 save          your saved games
 c, s          only for booting an emulator from the drawer (above)


 PROBLEMS
 --------

 The version is shown at the bottom of the main menu. Please give it with
 any report, so we know which build you were playing.

 THIS PACKAGE COMES WITH NO WARRANTY OF ANY KIND. USE IT AT YOUR OWN RISK.


